> simplify tan(x)^2 + 1 - 1/cos(x)^2
  ucas: trig tan(x)^2 + 1 - 1/cos(x)^2
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of tan(x)^2 + 1 - 1/cos(x)^2
  in sin and cos: tan = sin/cos, sec = 1/cos, csc = 1/sin, cot = cos/sin, tanh = sinh/cosh
    = 0
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-14)
  exponential (Euler): cos u = (e^(iu) + e^(-iu))/2, tan u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(i(e^(iu) + e^(-iu)))
    = ((exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))/(i*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))))^2 + 1 - 1/((exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))/2)^2
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-14)
  simplest: 0  (in sin and cos)
