> simplify atan(tan(x))
  ucas: trig atan(tan(x))
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of atan(tan(x))
  simplified: sin^2 + cos^2 = 1, cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1, f(f^-1(u)) = u
    = x
    for -pi/2 < x < pi/2
    check: equal at 38 of 64 sample points where -pi/2 < x < pi/2
      (outside: differs at 26 of 26 points, so the condition is needed)
  in sin and cos: tan = sin/cos, sec = 1/cos, csc = 1/sin, cot = cos/sin, tanh = sinh/cosh
    = atan(sin(x)/cos(x))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  atan via asin: atan(u) = asin(u/sqrt(1 + u^2))
    = asin(tan(x)/sqrt(tan(x)^2 + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 6e-16)
  atan via acos: atan(u) = sign(u)*acos(1/sqrt(1 + u^2))
    = sign(tan(x))*acos(1/sqrt(tan(x)^2 + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 6e-16)
  atan reflection: atan(u) = pi/2 - atan(1/u)
    = pi/2 - atan(1/tan(x))
    for (tan(x)) > 0
    check: equal at 30 of 64 sample points where (tan(x)) > 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 34 of 34 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan reflection: atan(u) = -pi/2 - atan(1/u)
    = -pi/2 - atan(1/tan(x))
    for (tan(x)) < 0
    check: equal at 34 of 64 sample points where (tan(x)) < 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 30 of 30 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan half-angle: atan(u) = 2atan(u/(1 + sqrt(1 + u^2)))
    = 2atan(tan(x)/(sqrt(tan(x)^2 + 1) + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  atan as atan2: atan(u) = atan2(u, 1)
    = atan2(tan(x), 1)
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
  logarithmic and exponential (Euler): tan u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(i(e^(iu) + e^(-iu))), atan u = (i/2) log((1 - iu)/(1 + iu))
    = i*log((1 - i*(exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))/(i*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))))/(i*(exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))/(i*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))) + 1))/2
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  simplest: atan2(tan(x), 1)  (atan as atan2)
> simplify arcsin(sin(x))
  ucas: trig arcsin(sin(x))
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of arcsin(sin(x))
  simplified: sin^2 + cos^2 = 1, cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1, f(f^-1(u)) = u
    = x
    for -pi/2 <= x <= pi/2
    check: equal at 38 of 64 sample points where -pi/2 <= x <= pi/2 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 26 of 26 points, so the condition is needed)
  asin via atan: asin(u) = atan(u/sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = atan(sin(x)/sqrt(1 - sin(x)^2))
    for -1 < (sin(x)) < 1
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points where -1 < (sin(x)) < 1 (max relative difference 3e-16)
  asin via acos: asin(u) = pi/2 - acos(u)
    = pi/2 - acos(sin(x))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  asin via acos: asin(u) = acos(sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = acos(sqrt(1 - sin(x)^2))
    for 0 <= (sin(x)) <= 1
    check: equal at 38 of 64 sample points where 0 <= (sin(x)) <= 1 (max relative difference 4e-16)
      (outside: differs at 26 of 26 points, so the condition is needed)
  asin via acos: asin(u) = -acos(sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = -acos(sqrt(1 - sin(x)^2))
    for -1 <= (sin(x)) <= 0
    check: equal at 26 of 64 sample points where -1 <= (sin(x)) <= 0 (max relative difference 3e-16)
      (outside: differs at 38 of 38 points, so the condition is needed)
  asin half-angle: asin(u) = 2atan(u/(1 + sqrt(1 - u^2)))
    = 2atan(sin(x)/(sqrt(1 - sin(x)^2) + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-16)
  asin as atan2: asin(u) = atan2(u, sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = atan2(sin(x), sqrt(1 - sin(x)^2))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-16)
  logarithmic and exponential (Euler): sin u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(2i), asin u = -i log(iu + sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = -i*log(i*(exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))/(2*i) + sqrt(1 - ((exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))/(2*i))^2))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-16)
  simplest: arcsin(sin(x))  (as given)
